.TH DLPI-MAC 1M "30 October 2026" "amix-base"
.SH NAME
dlpi-mac \- print the station address of a network interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dlpi-mac
[
.B \-p
.I ppa
] [
.B \-s
.I sap
] [
.B \-t
.I seconds
]
.I device
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dlpi-mac
prints the station (MAC) address of the Ethernet interface whose DLPI
device is
.IR device ,
such as
.B /dev/aen0
or
.BR /dev/zen0 ,
as six two-digit hexadecimal numbers joined by colons:
.PP
.nf
.ft CW
00:80:10:ff:ff:ff
.ft R
.fi
.PP
Nothing else is printed on the standard output, so a script can use it as
it is.
It works the same way with every DLPI Ethernet driver and needs no
driver-specific code.
It may be run before or after the interface is set up: it sends no frame
and leaves the device as it found it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p " ppa"
the physical point of attachment to attach to, for a driver that needs one
(DLPI Style 2); default 0.
.TP
.BI \-s " sap"
the service access point (Ethernet type) to bind while asking; default
0x88B5, a type no protocol uses.
.TP
.BI \-t " seconds"
how long to wait for each answer from the driver; default 5.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
the address was printed.
.TP
1
a usage error, or the device could not be opened (no such card in this
machine).
.TP
2
the driver did not answer as DLPI requires, or not in time.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR interfaces (4)
